*** After a 1NT overcall

A double of the 1NT overcall is for penalty (9+ hcp: opener's 12+ makes the
partnership's majority of the values); a two-level suit is a weak, natural
escape with a five-card suit.

1X-(1N)-
D = 9+ hcp
2Y = 0--8 hcp, 5+#

** Responses to a double of our opening

If RHO doubles our opening, a new suit response is forcing regardless of point
count (but capped below redouble's own 10+ hcp, so the two do not compete for
the same hand); a two-level bid is non-forcing (6--10, usually a six-card suit,
written here with that suit so parallel two-level bids stay disjoint); 2NT is a
limit raise or better in opener's suit (4+ trumps); redouble shows 10+ points
without that fit; a single raise is 6--9 and a jump raise is preemptive with
good support but fewer than 10 points; 1NT is a natural 6--9 without a fit; a jump
shift is to play, showing a six-plus card suit.

