(1Y)-1Z-(P)-
2X = {prio:1} NF, 10+ hcp, 5+#, 0--2Z

After the cuebid, the overcaller rebids the suit with a minimum (the booklet's
cuebid asks about the overcall's quality, and a minimum overcall has nothing
else to say), bids 2NT with extra values and a stopper, and jumps in the suit
with extra values otherwise; the three calls cover every hand, since the
cuebid is forcing. The same answers apply when opener's partner has doubled
in between.

