** Sandwich position: both opponents have bid

After an opening and a response by the opponents (partner having passed), a
double is for takeout of the two unbid suits (12+, at most three cards in either
of their suits), a suit bid is a natural overcall with a five-card suit (10+ at
the two level), and 1NT is a natural 15--18 with a stopper. A double of their 1NT
response is for penalty. Several tables share one position here because each
names the overcall's suit by a different variable: `Y` in `(1X)-P-(1Y)-` is
above the response is `Z` in `(1X)-P-(1Z)-` (between opener and responder) and so
on, a `Y` binding only reaching suits above `X` (NOTES.md #C3).

