** Over the opponents' 1NT opening

The booklet gives no conventional defense to a 1NT opening, so it is played
natural: a double is for penalty (15+, a hand at least as good as the
opener's), and a two-level suit bid is a natural overcall with a five-card suit.

(1N)-
D = {prio:1} 15+ hcp
2X = 8--15 hcp, 5+#

Advancing the natural two-level overcall (NOTES.md #C5): opposite a 15--17 opener
there is no game unless advancer has an opening hand, so a fit with 8--11 raises
to the three level (competing), game is bid with 12+ (the major with a fit,
otherwise 3NT), a six-card suit of advancer's own with shortness in the
overcall is a signoff, and anything else passes. If the opener's partner
competes, advancer still raises with a fit and doubles for penalty with 10+.

